data dynatron_df126025bu_pwmh_ref: DeclarationRef = DeclarationRef {
  module_path: "extdeps.fans.dynatron",
  decl_name: "dynatron_df126025bu_pwmh_catalog",
  field: WholeDeclaration,
}

// THE 2U CHASSIS BAYS DERIVE THEIR PART FROM ONE DECLARATION, AND THE ARM IS OperatorDeclaredPart
// RATHER THAN LabelObserved. The operator stated the model in their own words against an ARCTIC P8
// PWM PST listing, which is a statement about the machines they run and not a label read off a hub
// with the case open. That is the weaker of the two arms and it is chosen deliberately: this
// binding may pick a curve or order a spare, and physical_inventory_confirmation refuses it for the
// inventory question.
//
// THE DECLARANT, DATE, QUOTATION, PROMPT AND SCOPE NOW LIVE IN gunbc.operator_fan_declaration
// RATHER THAN IN THIS COMMENT. They previously sat here as prose beside six rows that each authored
// the declared arm independently, so the six agreed only because one author wrote them in one
// sitting - a seventh row on an undeclared 4U bay would have contradicted nothing a machine could
// read. The scope is now consulted per header, so a bay outside it cannot inhabit the declared arm.
//
// THE CLAIM WAS HELD UNBOUND FOR A DAY WHILE THE PROVENANCE WAS UNRESOLVED, and the reason is on
// the record because it is the failure this axis exists to prevent. A review round asserted the
// operator had already declared this model; no user turn in the session's transcript contained the
// statement, and the reviewer withdrew the attribution on the grounds that a first-person message
// in a relayed channel establishes who SUBMITTED bytes and not who authored them. Minting the row
// then would have put a fabricated citation in the inventory carrier -- the kind that reads correct
// forever because nothing re-derives it.
//
// THE DECLARATION IS SCOPED TO THE 2U CHASSIS, AND THAT IS WHY THERE ARE TWO HELPERS RATHER THAN
// ONE. The operator named the 80mm fans in the 2U machines. srv1 and srv2 are 4U with a different
// bay size, and the same helper served all four hosts -- so binding the part inside the shared
// helper would have asserted an ARCTIC P8 in srv1's and srv2's 4U bays, which nobody declared and
// which the frame size alone makes unlikely. A declaration is scoped to what was said about.
//
// NOT-DAISY-CHAINED DOES NOT ESTABLISH ONE FAN PER HEADER, AND BOTH HELPERS PREVIOUSLY ASSERTED
// THAT IT DID. Each carried DrivenFanCountOperatorDeclared { count: 1 } and a tach representation
// of exactly one rotor, on the strength of "they are not daisy chained today, nothign is". PWM
// Sharing Technology chains fan to fan, so the statement rules that topology out - and a Y-splitter
// or a powered hub puts two fans on one header without any fan-to-fan chain at all. THIS FLEET
// CONTAINS SUCH A SPLITTER: srv1 and srv2 drive FAN1 through the NA-YC1 that ships with the
// NH-D9 AMP-4926. So the operator's sentence is true of a fleet that demonstrably has a splitter in
// it, which refutes the inference by counter-example from this module's own rows rather than by
// argument about what they might have meant.
//
// The tach half was the same overreach one level down, and it is the mistake this module already
// corrected for srv1's FAN1: a BMC publishing one rpm value establishes that the header CARRIES a
// signal and nothing about how many rotors that signal speaks for. Reading a live tach as
// "represented_fan_count: 1" is exactly the inference the splitter case exists to refuse, so
// applying it to the P8 bays used a stronger evidence reading than the fleet's own known topology
// permits.
fn chassis_bay_wiring(header: NonEmptyStr) -> FanHeaderWiring {
  FanHeaderWiring {
    header: header,
    driven_fan_count: DrivenFanCountUnobserved,
    model: FanModelUnobserved,
    tach_source: TachCarriedByDrivenFan { representation: TachRepresentationUnobserved },
  }
}

// THE SCOPE DECIDES THE ARM, so a header the declaration does not reach falls back to unobserved
// instead of quietly inheriting the declared part from its neighbours.
fn chassis_bay_wiring_2u(host: HostIdentity, header: NonEmptyStr) -> FanHeaderWiring {
  FanHeaderWiring {
    header: header,
    driven_fan_count: DrivenFanCountUnobserved,
    model: match declaration_reach(
      declaration: arctic_p8_2u_chassis_declaration,
      host: host,
      header: header,
    ) {
      DeclarationCoversHeader =>
        FanModelOperatorDeclaredPart { catalog: arctic_p8_2u_chassis_declaration.model }
      other => FanModelUnobserved
    },
    tach_source: TachCarriedByDrivenFan { representation: TachRepresentationUnobserved },
  }
}

// srv1/srv2 FAN1 IS AN ASSEMBLY EXPECTATION, NOT AN OBSERVATION, and this block previously said
// the opposite on an argument that its own module now refutes. It read: five live tach channels
// prove the splitter is not in use, "because a splitter suppresses one tach entirely". The NA-YC1
// omits the RPM conductor on ONE branch precisely so the other still reports, so four chassis
// headers plus one cooler header behind a splitter produce five channels too. The evidence was
// consistent with both realizations and was read as deciding between them.
//
// What is actually known: the NH-D9 AMP-4926 4U ships two NF-A9 HS-PWM fans and an NA-YC1
// splitter, and FAN1 publishes a live rpm value. What is NOT known, because nobody has opened
// these two machines: how many fans hang off FAN1, and how many rotors its one signal speaks for.
// The parent authority already says exactly this, so asserting 2 and 1 here made the child
// contradict the module it builds on while looking like a refinement of it.
data srv1_fan_wiring: HostFanWiring = HostFanWiring {
  host: operator_host_srv1,
  headers: [
    FanHeaderWiring {
      header: "FAN1",
      driven_fan_count: DrivenFanCountDerivedFromAssembly {
        expected_count: 2,
        specification: noctua_nh_d9_amp_4926_bundled_fan,
      },
      model: FanModelDerivedFromAssembly { specification: noctua_nh_d9_amp_4926_bundled_fan },
      tach_source: TachCarriedByDrivenFan { representation: TachRepresentationUnobserved },
    },
    chassis_bay_wiring(header: "FAN2"),
    chassis_bay_wiring(header: "FAN3"),
    chassis_bay_wiring(header: "FAN4"),
    chassis_bay_wiring(header: "FAN5"),
  ],
}

data srv2_fan_wiring: HostFanWiring = HostFanWiring {
  host: operator_host_srv2,
  headers: [
    FanHeaderWiring {
      header: "FAN1",
      driven_fan_count: DrivenFanCountDerivedFromAssembly {
        expected_count: 2,
        specification: noctua_nh_d9_amp_4926_bundled_fan,
      },
      model: FanModelDerivedFromAssembly { specification: noctua_nh_d9_amp_4926_bundled_fan },
      tach_source: TachCarriedByDrivenFan { representation: TachRepresentationUnobserved },
    },
    chassis_bay_wiring(header: "FAN2"),
    chassis_bay_wiring(header: "FAN3"),
    chassis_bay_wiring(header: "FAN4"),
    chassis_bay_wiring(header: "FAN5"),
  ],
}

// srv3/srv4: the Dynatron W1 carries ONE DF126025BU-PWMH. The three chassis fans are the ones
// Rosewill preinstalls in the RSV-Z2600U and nobody has read a part number off them, so they
// stand at FanModelUnobserved - which costs nothing downstream, because both derivations below
// ignore model standing entirely.
data srv3_fan_wiring: HostFanWiring = HostFanWiring {
  host: operator_host_srv3,
  headers: [
    FanHeaderWiring {
      header: "FAN1",
      driven_fan_count: DrivenFanCountDerivedFromAssembly {
        expected_count: 1,
        specification: dynatron_w1_bundled_fan,
      },
      model: FanModelDerivedFromAssembly { specification: dynatron_w1_bundled_fan },
      tach_source: TachCarriedByDrivenFan {
        representation: TachRepresentationObserved { represented_fan_count: 1 },
      },
    },
    chassis_bay_wiring_2u(host: operator_host_srv3, header: "FAN3"),
    chassis_bay_wiring_2u(host: operator_host_srv3, header: "FAN4"),
    chassis_bay_wiring_2u(host: operator_host_srv3, header: "FAN5"),
  ],
}

data srv4_fan_wiring: HostFanWiring = HostFanWiring {
  host: operator_host_srv4,
  headers: [
    FanHeaderWiring {
      header: "FAN1",
      driven_fan_count: DrivenFanCountDerivedFromAssembly {
        expected_count: 1,
        specification: dynatron_w1_bundled_fan,
      },
      model: FanModelDerivedFromAssembly { specification: dynatron_w1_bundled_fan },
      tach_source: TachCarriedByDrivenFan {
        representation: TachRepresentationObserved { represented_fan_count: 1 },
      },
    },
    chassis_bay_wiring_2u(host: operator_host_srv4, header: "FAN2"),
    chassis_bay_wiring_2u(host: operator_host_srv4, header: "FAN3"),
    chassis_bay_wiring_2u(host: operator_host_srv4, header: "FAN4"),
